```cs
[Test]
public void TestLastIndexOfContract()
{
    // Arrange
    ArrayList arrList = new ArrayList();
    arrList.Add(1);
    arrList.Add(2);
    arrList.Add(3);
    int x = 2;
    int old_arrList_LastIndexOf_x = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    // Act
    int new_arrList_LastIndexOf_x = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    // Assert
    Assert.IsTrue(new_arrList_LastIndexOf_x >= 0); // @@@ If the return value is positive, return value is at least the index of x in old list 
}
```
The assert statement asserts that the return value of `arrList.LastIndexOf(x)` is positive. The index returned by `arrList.LastIndexOf(x)` is considered as the index of `x` in the original list (`old_arrList_LastIndexOf_x`). In this case, the `LastIndexOf` method will return the highest index of the value `x` within `arrList`. As such, if the index is positive, it means that `x` is found at least once in `arrList`.
